{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778538977,"nonce":"Fg2qhs1iHDeIeAeofpdLyvL6zKQ=","title":"Auto-register MCP channel server with Claude Code on install","message":"Currently, registering Mandible's MCP channel server with Claude Code requires a manual `claude mcp add` command (or manual edit of `~/.claude.json`). This is fragile — the user must know the exact path to `dist/channel-server/index.js` and the correct scope/transport flags.\n\nWhen Mandible is distributed as a standalone app (Tauri Level 2, `fdc0e8a`), installation should automatically register the channel server with Claude Code's MCP configuration. For the current dev-install case, `mandible setup` (or equivalent) should handle it.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. **Auto-registration on install/setup**: `mandible setup` (or Tauri installer) writes the `mcpServers.mandible` entry to `~/.claude.json` with scope `user` (all projects). Uses `claude mcp add --scope user --transport stdio mandible -- node \u003cpath\u003e/dist/channel-server/index.js` if the CLI is available, or writes directly to `~/.claude.json` as fallback.\n2. **Unregistration on uninstall**: Removes the entry cleanly.\n3. **Settings UI toggle**: The Mandible settings dashboard should expose an \"Enable Claude Code MCP integration\" toggle that registers/unregisters the channel server. This lets users activate or deactivate the integration without manual CLI commands.\n4. **Idempotency**: Re-running setup or toggling the setting on when already registered is a no-op (no duplicates, no errors).\n5. **Path resolution**: The registered path must resolve correctly regardless of where Mandible is installed. For Tauri sidecar, this is the bundled JS path; for dev installs, the repo's `dist/channel-server/index.js`.\n\n## Context\n\nSurfaced from the dotfiles wiring work (`9c8daf7`). The initial attempt put `mcpServers` in `~/.claude/settings.json`, which is the wrong file — Claude Code reads MCP servers from `~/.claude.json`. This footgun would be eliminated by having Mandible handle its own registration.\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- `9c8daf7` (dotfiles wiring — needs partial revert to remove invalid mcpServers from settings.json)\n- `4e32923` (channel server implementation)\n- `497fafa` (notify script migration)\n- `fdc0e8a` (Tauri Level 2)\n- `c58acc8` (settings UI)\n- rlrmp meta coord: `1d9ae6f`","files":null}]}